<th id="S3.T2.5.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">512</th>
<td id="S3.T2.5.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">97.26</td>
<td id="S3.T2.5.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">73.34</td>
<td id="S3.T2.5.3.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">98.04</td></tr>
<tr id="S3.T2.5.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S3.T2.5.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Google VIT</th>
<th id="S3.T2.5.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row">768</th>
<td id="S3.T2.5.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">99.88</td>
<td id="S3.T2.5.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">91.62</td>
<td id="S3.T2.5.4.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">98.98</td></tr>
<tr id="S3.T2.5.5" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S3.T2.5.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">DinoV2</th>
<th id="S3.T2.5.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row">768</th>
<td id="S3.T2.5.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">100.00</td>
<td id="S3.T2.5.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">99.62</td>
<td id="S3.T2.5.5.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">99.94</td></tr>
<tr id="S3.T2.5.6" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S3.T2.5.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">ResNet-50</th>
<th id="S3.T2.5.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row">2048</th>
<td id="S3.T2.5.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">99.89</td>
<td id="S3.T2.5.6.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">84.02</td>
<td id="S3.T2.5.6.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">98.47</td></tr>
<tr id="S3.T2.5.7" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S3.T2.5.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_b">AIMV2</th>
<th id="S3.T2.5.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_b">1024</th>
<td id="S3.T2.5.7.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b">99.96</td>
<td id="S3.T2.5.7.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b">92.59</td>
<td id="S3.T2.5.7.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b">99.81</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="S3.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">The blur analysis reveals a systematic relationship between blur intensity and model performance, as detailed in Table <a href="#S3.T3" title="TABLE III ‣ III-B Benchmarking different embedding models ‣ III Evaluation ‣ Provenance of AI-Generated Images: A Vector Similarity and Blockchain-based Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">III</span></a>. At low blur levels (20%), most models maintained robust performance, with DinoV2 achieving perfect accuracy and both Google ViT and AIMv2 exceeding 99% accuracy. However, as the blur intensity increased, we can observe a consistent degradation pattern across all models, though at varying rates. DinoV2 demonstrated remarkable resilience, maintaining 88.44% accuracy even at 80% blur intensity, significantly outperforming other models. In contrast, ResNet-50, despite its larger embedding dimension of 2048, shows the highest sensitivity to blur effects, with accuracy dropping dramatically to 24.67% at 80% blur.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S3.T3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">TABLE III</span>: </span><span id="S3.T3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Model Accuracy (%) Under Various Blur Intensities</span></figcaption>
<table id="S3.T3.5" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
